# Cowboy

**Alignments.** Any.

The average cowboy is an expert in roping, riding and driving cattle, horses
and similar livestock, buffalo included. One in four is a Psi-Stalker, one in
six a D-bee, one in eight a Mexican or Indian, one in ten a partial or full
conversion cyborg, and one in a hundred a supernatural being or a practitioner
of magic, usually low to mid level. Only one in ten is female.

Cowboys are found wherever ranches and cattle trails are thickest: the
territories once called Texas, Oklahoma, Kansas, Nebraska, New Mexico,
Colorado, Wyoming, Montana and South Dakota, and the Coalition States of
Missouri and Arkansas.

## The horse

A cowboy''s horse is always of very good to excellent quality and well trained.
Before the Rifts the horse was usually lent to him by his employer; in the New
West most cowboys, and certainly those who travel from job to job and take up
adventuring, own their own. A few keep a hovercycle or a robot horse instead,
but most would rather have the animal - the book quotes a pre-Rifts cowboy to
the effect that a man on foot is no man at all, and a dismounted cowboy is just
a bow-legged human who smells of horse.

## Lore

Also known as the Cowhand, the Cowpoke, the Wrangler and the Buckaroo.
